# Support Ticket Console Manager

A Java console application for managing customer support tickets as part of Mablewave SIWES assignment.

## Features
1. Create Ticket - Log new customer issues with client name, priority, and assigned staff
2. View Tickets - Display all tickets in a formatted list
3. Update Ticket Status - Change status between OPEN, IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVED, CLOSED
4. Search Ticket - Search by ID or client name
5. Ticket Summary - View counts of total, open, resolved, and high/critical tickets
6. Exit

## How to Run
1. Open the project in IntelliJ IDEA or any Java IDE
2. Run `src/main/java/Main.java`
3. Use the menu to navigate options 1-6

## Project Structure
## Concepts Used
- Object Oriented Programming: Classes, encapsulation, enums
- Collections: ArrayList for storing tickets
- Exception Handling: Try-catch for invalid input
- Java Streams: For filtering and counting in summary
- Package organization

## Notes
Data is stored in memory only. Closing the program will clear all tickets.